{"id": "EUVD-2026-76633", "enisaUuid": "26b9122c-23dc-37ea-be42-221238689ac1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nphy: rockchip-samsung-dcphy: fix out-of-range max_register\n\nThe PHY register block is 64KB, so with a register stride of 4 the\nlast accessible register sits at offset 0xfffc. max_register names\n0x10000, one register past the end of the mapping: dumping the\nregisters through the regmap debugfs interface reads beyond the\nioremapped region and oopses on the unmapped page. The oops fires\nwith the regmap lock held, so later PHY operations deadlock.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:51:33", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/14afe18655c0951f4f85898f761bf92264e65ccd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c1a62f9dcf531d56c56da2e4435386b6d264c69f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4486e75ba647bd8b98fc1f053101b40caceeed4b"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jrrm-mv6f-g3m6", "CVE-2026-89721"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6bac27cf-65ad-31c4-90b0-e3ff9507ba6c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "732ef9ca-eea4-378c-b781-b54728f2c8bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8b016840-1baa-3b26-935c-ec50bd7c38e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b2a1a2ae7818c9d8da12bf7b1983c8b9f5fb712b <14afe18655c0951f4f85898f761bf92264e65ccd"}, {"id": "a16122b4-6cb6-35b1-bdb8-93f225d97fe0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b2a1a2ae7818c9d8da12bf7b1983c8b9f5fb712b <c1a62f9dcf531d56c56da2e4435386b6d264c69f"}, {"id": "be05d434-5611-3e53-963d-b13db4a8877e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b2a1a2ae7818c9d8da12bf7b1983c8b9f5fb712b <4486e75ba647bd8b98fc1f053101b40caceeed4b"}, {"id": "dc6